        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-1: Instead of checking if deleting a single character results in a valid word, modify the approach to directly compare each word with every possible word formed by deleting one character. For each word, generate all substrings obtained by removing one character and check if any of these substrings exist in the dictionary. If so, mark the original word as a typo. This method ensures accurate identification of typos without relying on a potentially flawed single-character deletion search within the Trie.",
